1.7 Faster node search
======================

When you invoke ‘org-roam-node-find’, Emacs has to build the list of
every node in your database before you can start typing.  On a large
database this pause is long enough to interrupt your flow.  The delay
comes from how each node's display line is constructed: org-roam uses a
format string with ‘%’-placeholders, and assembling that string for
every node on every invocation is slow.

   ‘org-roam-gt’ replaces the format string with a plain Lisp function
that produces the same display but runs faster, which shortens the pause
noticeably.  The completion interface looks and behaves identically.
The original template is restored if you disable the mode.


